{"call_id":"call_LahmYyZduCRlrGonIrfQfs6z","event_id":"ctco_01a08fdd-589f-7a32-8832-355e485da0ba","output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"30b510\",\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2204,\"output\":\"../git-meta/crates/git-meta-cli/src/cli.rs:22:pub(crate) enum Commands {\\n../git-meta/crates/git-meta-cli/src/cli.rs:275:    Setup,\\n../git-meta/crates/git-meta-cli/src/cli.rs:586:        heading: \\\"setup and configuration\\\",\\n../git-meta/crates/git-meta-cli/src/cli.rs:589:            commands: &[\\\"setup\\\", \\\"remote\\\", \\\"config\\\", \\\"teardown\\\"],\\n../git-meta/spec/implementation/cli.md:162:## Setup and configuration\\n../git-meta/spec/implementation/cli.md:168:### Setup\\n../git-meta/spec/implementation/cli.md:171:git meta setup\\n../git-meta/spec/implementation/cli.md:185:setup fields without breaking older clients.\\n../git-meta/spec/implementation/cli.md:286:`git meta setup` (or `git meta remote add`) re-installs the local\\n\\nThe tree root is `refs/meta/local/main^{tree}`. The compiler produces real Git blob, tree, and parent-linked commit SHA-1 IDs, `__value`, `__set`, timestamped `__list` entries, branch hash prefixes, and escaped `path/.../__target__` directories. Keys beginning with `local:` stay out of the exchange tree. Strings preserve their raw text; the demonstration's set/list `value` accepts comma-separated members. Sets deduplicate members; lists preserve their order.\\n\\nThe example snapshot in `examples/git-meta/serializer-reference.json` records reference data from `/tmp/meta-demo`; it resolves the example's short target commit IDs and preserves list timestamps while keeping the packaged demo independent of that repository. The commit sidebar shows the demonstration's metadata snapshots. The interactive demonstration stays in memory and does not modify the source repository or SQLite database.\\n\\nArrow keys continue the presentation. Returning to the component preserves its current tree; leaving the station or logging out clears it. Run `node scripts/check-serializer.mjs --packaged` to exercise the native desktop interactions after packaging.\\n\\n`<Scalar />` opens **gitviz**, an SGI-style desktop visualizer at station 07.\\nIt steps through two writes, a prune commit, a full push, User 2's partial setup,\\na missing-object lookup, and an on-demand fetch. Purple commits point to teal trees; gold cubes are local\\nblobs. Dashed A/B boxes on User 2 indicate promised objects. The prune preserves\\nhistorical trees and blobs; setup gets C/D, and reading k1 fetches only A.\\n\\nUse Space/Right and Left to move through the seven steps, or click the step list.\\nR resets, B steps back, and P toggles playback. Tilt, Zoom, and Speed sliders\\ncontrol the view and playback; **bird's eye** and **front view** are presets.\\nAt either end, arrows continue to the adjacent presentation page. **Session**\\nor the title-bar minimize button restores park control. Returning to the page\\npreserves state; leaving the station or logging out clears it. Each visited\\nScalar step counts toward Power progress.\\n\\nAn optional `title` prop changes the window title. The demo is an in-memory\\npresentation: displayed `git meta` commands follow `../git-meta`'s CLI, but do\\nnot execute against a repository. A–D, C1–C3 and T1–T3 are readable aliases;\\nnested Git path trees and metadata bookkeeping are omitted. All four keys use\\n`path:demo`. Explicit `set --timestamp` values date k1/k2 to August 31, 2026 and\\nk3/k4 to September 11, so `prune --since 2026-09-01` retains exactly C/D.\\nSetup assumes `.git-meta` names the shared remote without a depth limit.\\n\\nRun `node scripts/check-scalar.mjs` for the native interaction test, or add\\n`--packaged` after packaging. It captures add, prune, setup, and read screenshots\\nin `unreal/Saved/Screenshots/`.\\n\\nScalar renders real native meshes into its desktop viewport. Commit, tree, and\\nblob labels are inset onto their top planes, with no commit timestamps. Drag\\nthe viewport to orbit and scroll to zoom. **Camera: moving camera** follows\\neach step's action; click it (or press C) for **full scene**, which keeps all\\nthree spaces framed. Mouse orbit works in both modes.\\n\\nPush animates ten object copies to the remote (three commits, three trees,\\nfour blobs). Setup animates eight copies to User 2 (three commits, three trees,\\nC and D). The get step first shows the missing A lookup; the following step\\nanimates A's promisor fetch and returns its value. Source objects stay in place,\\nand B stays remote. Autoplay lets each transfer finish before advancing.\\n#pragma once\\n#include \\\"CoreMinimal.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"Styling/SlateBrush.h\\\"\\nclass UMaterialInstanceDynamic;\\nclass UWorld;class AActor;class ASceneCapture2D;class USceneComponent;class UPrimitiveComponent;class UWidgetComponent;class UStaticMeshComponent;class FParkScalar;\\n\\n// An isolated native scene rendered into the desktop's viewport.\\nclass FParkScalarScene {\\n TWeakObjectPtr<AActor> Actor;\\n TWeakObjectPtr<ASceneCapture2D> Capture;\\n TArray<TWeakObjectPtr<USceneComponent>> Objects;\\n TMap<uint64,TWeakObjectPtr<UMaterialInstanceDynamic>> ColorMaterials;\\n UStaticMeshComponent* Box(FVector Center,FVector Size,FColor Color,bool Dynamic=true,bool Lit=true);\\n void Link(FVector From,FVector To,FColor Color,float Width=3,bool Dashed=false,bool Dynamic=true);\\n UWidgetComponent* Label(FVector Center,FVector2D Size,const TArray<FString>& Lines,FColor Color=FColor::White);\\n void Rebuild(const FParkScalar& State);\\n struct FTransfer {TWeakObjectPtr<USceneComponent> Component;FVector Destination;};\\n TArray<FTransfer> Transfers;\\n float TransferOffset=0;\\n void TrackTransfer(int32 Start,float Offset);\\n int32 BuiltStep=-1;\\n boo